WEBVTT

00:02:58.758 --> 00:03:01.469
they'll respond with a list
of activities that they enjoy.

00:03:01.510 --> 00:03:05.348
You know, they'll say, "Dancing is fun,"
or "Skiing is fun," or, I don't know,

00:03:05.348 --> 00:03:07.266
"Pickleball is fun."

00:03:08.100 --> 00:03:11.437
Everyone seems to think
that pickleball is fun.

00:03:11.437 --> 00:03:14.482
(Cheers and laughter)

00:03:14.523 --> 00:03:16.776
And sure, pickleball can be fun,

00:03:16.817 --> 00:03:19.278
but we've all had experiences
where something's off,

00:03:19.320 --> 00:03:21.530
and an activity that seems
like it would be fun

00:03:21.530 --> 00:03:23.157
doesn't end up feeling fun.

00:03:23.199 --> 00:03:24.450
And then on the flip side,

00:03:24.492 --> 00:03:28.287
we've had experiences where something
that doesn't seem like it'll be fun at all

00:03:28.287 --> 00:03:29.914
ends up feeling ridiculously fun.

00:03:29.956 --> 00:03:31.749
There's an element of serendipity.